/target

# pkg/ (the wasm-pack output) is committed intentionally: the server consumes it
# at runtime and the Docker image has no Rust toolchain to rebuild it. Run
# `bun run build` (or `wasm-pack build --target nodejs --release`) to regenerate.
# Note: wasm-pack drops a `pkg/.gitignore` containing `*` on each build — delete
# it after rebuilding so the regenerated output stays tracked.
